{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5409: \"[stitch] cmd/date: srd060 R2.1-R2.4\". The task requires implementing/completing requirements R2.1 through R2.4 from `srd060-date.yaml` in the `cmd/date` utility. These requirements cover date string parsing via the `-d`/`--date` flag:\n   - R2.1: `-d STRING` or `--date=STRING` must display the date described by STRING instead of current time\n   - R2.2: Must parse epoch timestamps prefixed with `@` (e.g., `-d @1234567890`)\n   - R2.3: Must parse ISO 8601 date strings (e.g., `-d '2024-01-15 10:30:00'`)\n   - R2.4: When the date string cannot be parsed, must print error to stderr and exit 1\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/date/main.go` and `cmd/date/date_test.go`. Design decisions require extending (not reorganizing) existing code, adding new DiffTest entries, and using `LC_ALL=C` in all tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (`gdate`) via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   - SIGPIPE handler requirement for all cmd/ utilities\n   - strftime-style format string parsing\n   - Date string parsing: epoch (`@seconds`), ISO 8601, error handling\n   - Go `time` package for date parsing with `time.ParseInLocation`\n   - Git is managed externally - no git commands allowed\n   - `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/` convention\n   - LC_ALL=C for deterministic test output\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd060-date.yaml`\n     - Full SRD for cmd/date with 4 requirement groups (R1-R4)\n     - R2 group is the focus: \"Date string parsing (-d/--date)\"\n     - Non-goals: no `-s/--set`, no `--rfc-3339/--rfc-email`, no relative date strings (\"yesterday\", \"2 days ago\")\n   \n   - `cmd/date/main.go` (267 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Header claims: `// Implements srd060-date R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3.`\n     - **Already implements R2.1-R2.3**: `parseArgs` handles `-d`/`--date`/`--date=` (lines 50-57), `parseDateString` handles `@epoch` (lines 102-108) and ISO layouts (lines 95-113), `resolveTime` wires it together (lines 73-93)\n     - R2.4 error handling exists: `fmt.Errorf(\"invalid date '%s'\", s)` at line 114, propagated to stderr in main() at line 36-38\n     - Key date layouts: `\"2006-01-02 15:04:05\"`, `\"2006-01-02T15:04:05\"`, `\"2006-01-02\"`\n     - Full code preserved in conversation context above\n\n   - `cmd/date/date_test.go` (83 lines, existing tests)\n     - Has `setupBinaries` helper, uses `exec.LookPath(\"gdate\")`\n     - Has test functions: `TestDiffDefault`, `TestDiffFormatStrings`, `TestDiffSpecifiers`, `TestDiffGNUExtensions`\n     - Uses `Env: []string{\"TZ=UTC\"}` but NOT `LC_ALL=C` as D3 requires\n     - **Missing**: dedicated R2 group tests (date parsing, epoch, ISO 8601, error cases)\n     - Full code preserved in conversation context above\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted after file reads, before implementation.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key finding: The existing `main.go` already implements R2.1-R2.3 functionality. The main work needed is:\n     1. Update the file header comment to include R2.4 (or confirm R2.4 is covered)\n     2. Add dedicated differential tests for R2.1-R2.4 in `date_test.go`\n     3. Ensure `LC_ALL=C` is included in new test Env arrays per D3\n     4. Verify compilation and test passage\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive message containing the full task specification including: role definition, repository_files listing, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. The task is \"[stitch] cmd/date: srd060 R2.1-R2.4\".\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/date/main.go` to ensure R2.1-R2.4 are fully implemented (may need minimal changes since R2.1-R2.3 appear implemented; need to verify R2.4 error handling matches gdate behavior)\n   - Update file header comment to reflect R2.4\n   - Add a new test function (e.g., `TestDiffDateParsing`) to `cmd/date/date_test.go` with differential tests covering:\n     - `-d @epoch` variants (R2.2)\n     - `-d 'ISO 8601'` variants (R2.3)\n     - `--date=STRING` long form (R2.1)\n     - Invalid date strings with expected ExitCode: 1 (R2.4)\n   - All new tests must include `LC_ALL=C` in Env per D3\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/date/...` (AC1)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/date ./cmd/date/` (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/date/... -count=1` (AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (`srd060-date.yaml`, `cmd/date/main.go`, `cmd/date/date_test.go`) and was about to begin implementation. My analysis showed the existing main.go already has R2.1-R2.3 implemented, and R2.4 error handling appears present. The primary work is adding dedicated differential tests for the R2 group and potentially minor adjustments to main.go.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the implementation changes. Specifically:\n   1. Update `cmd/date/main.go` header comment to include R2.4 (change `R2.1-R2.3` to `R2.1-R2.4`)\n   2. Add a `TestDiffDateParsing` function to `cmd/date/date_test.go` with DiffTest entries covering:\n      - `-d @0` epoch zero (R2.2)\n      - `-d @1234567890` (R2.2)\n      - `--date=@1700000000` long form (R2.1)\n      - `-d '2024-01-15 10:30:00'` ISO 8601 with space (R2.3)\n      - `-d '2024-01-15T10:30:00'` ISO 8601 with T (R2.3)\n      - `-d '2024-01-15'` date-only ISO (R2.3)\n      - `-d 'invalid'` with ExitCode: 1 (R2.4)\n      